# Operator admin (Flowbite)

`/admin` is a **separate app shell** from the cabinet. Visual language: [Flowbite Admin Dashboard](https://github.com/themesberg/flowbite-admin-dashboard) utility classes. Administrate is gone.

## Two CSS worlds — never mix

| Surface | Entry | Classes |
|--------|--------|---------|
| Cabinet (`/`) | `tailwind` + daisyUI | `btn`, `alert`, `modal`, daisyUI colors |
| Admin (`/admin`) | `admin.css` + Flowbite plugin | Tailwind utilities + Flowbite plugin. **No** `btn` / `alert` / `modal` / daisyUI |

- Do not `import "flowbite"` / pin `flowbite.js`. Drawers, dropdowns, tabs = Stimulus.
- Light-only. No `dark:`, no theme toggle, no `class="dark"` on `<html>`.
- `data-turbo-track="reload"` on both CSS/JS. Links to cabinet (`root_path`, logout) keep `data-turbo="false"`.
- Admin views: `app/views/admin/**/*.html.erb`. Cabinet stays Slim + daisyUI.

Exception: advertising order **new/edit** load cabinet CSS via `content_for :head` and render shared Slim `_form` (order-grid). Index/show of orders stay Flowbite.

## Stack

- Controllers: `Admin::*Controller < Admin::BaseController` (`ActionController::Base`).
- Layout: `admin/operator` (`app/views/layouts/admin/operator.html.erb`). Extra CSS: `yield :head`.
- Auth: `Current.user.organization.operator?` — **no Pundit** in `/admin`.
- Importmap entry: `javascript_importmap_tags "admin"` → `app/javascript/admin.js`.
- Stimulus: `eagerLoadControllersFrom("admin/controllers", application)` under `app/javascript/admin/controllers/`. Cabinet controllers are not auto-loaded; `order-grid` is registered manually in `admin.js`.
- CSS: `app/assets/tailwind/admin.css` (`@plugin "flowbite/plugin"`, `source(none)` + explicit `@source` of admin views/JS). Build: `Procfile.dev` `admin_css` watch, or `bin/rails tailwindcss:build` (enhances `admin:css:build` → `app/assets/builds/admin.css`).
- Pagination: Kaminari `theme: "admin"` → `app/views/kaminari/admin/`.
- Search/sort: Ransack. Always `ransack_params` (hash-only; scalar `q` must not 500). Allowlist `ransackable_attributes` / `ransackable_associations` on the model.

## Chrome and helpers

Sidebar items live in `AdminHelper::NAV_SECTIONS` (`app/helpers/admin_helper.rb`; `NAV_ITEMS` is the flattened list), not in routes introspection. Adding a resource: **routes + NAV_SECTIONS + `admin.nav.*` i18n**.

Use helper classes, do not invent new button/input palettes:

- `admin_primary_button_class` / `admin_secondary_button_class` / `admin_danger_button_class`
- `admin_input_class` / `admin_select_class` / `admin_checkbox_class` / `admin_label_class`
- `admin_enum_label` / `admin_enum_options` (i18n `enums.<model>.<attr>.<key>`)
- `admin_link_to_record` / `admin_record_path` / `admin_attachment_name` / `admin_boolean`
- Flashes: `admin_flash_for(resource, action)` falls back to `admin.crud.*`

Shared partials: `app/views/admin/shared/` (`_sidebar`, `_navbar`, `_flash`, `_empty_state`, `_form_errors`, `_operating_hours_fields`).

i18n: `config/locales/mediateca.{ru,en}.yml` keys `admin.chrome.*`, `admin.crud.*`, `admin.nav.*`. Resource-specific keys optional; prefer `admin.crud` unless the copy is unique (tags, media plans, orders).

Confirm destroy: `data-turbo-confirm`. Redirects after mutate: `status: :see_other`. FK/restrict destroy: `destroy_with_restriction`.

## Nested constants

Inside `Admin::Directory::*`, always `::Directory::BusinessSphere`. Form: `form_with model: [:admin, record]` — **not** `[:admin, :directory, record]` (double-nests the path). Links: `admin_directory_business_sphere_path`.

## Generators

Does **not** create a model, migration, or routes. Existing files skipped unless `--force`.

```bash
bin/rails g admin:install
bin/rails g admin:scaffold Widget name:string
```

`admin:install` copies chrome (BaseController, layout, Stimulus, `admin.css`, Kaminari theme).

`admin:scaffold NAME [field:type …]`:

- `app/controllers/admin/<plural>_controller.rb` — Ransack + Kaminari, `params.expect`
- views `index show new edit _form` under `app/views/admin/<plural>/`
- `spec/requests/admin/<plural>_spec.rb`
- injects `ransackable_*` on an **existing** model

After scaffold, always:

1. `resources :…` inside `namespace :admin` in `config/routes.rb`
2. Sidebar entry in `AdminHelper::NAV_SECTIONS`
3. i18n `admin.nav.<key>` (and crud copy if not using `admin.crud`)
4. Align the generated controller with live `BaseController` (`ransack_params` / `destroy_with_restriction` already inherited — drop duplicates)
5. Prefer `render "admin/shared/form_errors"` over inlined error HTML

If you change chrome (helper classes, layout, navbar, BaseController), sync `lib/generators/admin/install/templates/`.

## Resource exceptions (do not “complete” CRUD)

| Resource | Admin surface |
|----------|----------------|
| Media assets | index / show / edit / destroy — **no upload** |
| Media plans | index / show + member `cancel` (DELETE) / `reschedule` — **no new/edit/destroy** |
| Advertising orders | index / show / new / create / edit / update + `activate` / `cancel` — **no destroy**; grid = cabinet form |
| Profiles | show only |
| Stations | agent token **display** (set/blank), not editable on the form |
| Screens | virtual `location_id`; operator org as owner is stored as `nil`; tags via `tag_ids`; `template_id` copies a portrait onto the screen; inherit hours toggle + `_operating_hours_fields` when not inheriting; `service_theme_id` and pick-strategy virtual attrs (`header_start_pick_strategy`, `header_end_pick_strategy`, `welcome_pick_strategy`, `close_pick_strategy`) call `Portraits::ApplyServiceTheme` |
| Service themes | full CRUD + nested clip upload; four `system_managed` rotations stay off the ordinary Rotations index |
| Locations | `operating_hours` jsonb + Stimulus `operating-hours` |

HasMany on forms is opt-in (screen tags, group `screen_ids`, nested organization profile). Do not dump every association onto the form.

## Stimulus already in admin

- `sidebar`, `dropdown`, `modal`, `tabs` (chrome)
- `operating-hours` — copy Monday on location form
- `screen-form` — filter stations by location, inherit-hours toggle, optional name autofill (`data-auto-fill-name`)
- `portrait-blocks` — add/reorder portrait blocks; pick strategy visible for filler, insertion, headers, welcome, close

New interactivity: a small controller in `app/javascript/admin/controllers/`, not Flowbite JS.

## Tests

Docker only: `docker compose exec -e RAILS_ENV=test web bundle exec rspec spec/requests/admin spec/system/admin spec/generators`.

Chrome check: HTML includes `/assets/admin-`, does **not** include `app-container` / `navigation__link` / `administrate`. Submit admin forms with `within("main")` so navbar locale `button_to` is not clicked.
